.TH WAXEN 1 "November 10, 2026" "waxen 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
waxen \- find out whether macOS is right about an app it won't open
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B waxen
.I target
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B waxen
.B diagnose
.I target
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B waxen
.B evidence
.I target
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B waxen finder
.RB { install | uninstall }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B waxen
checks an application bundle or a download container (.dmg or .pkg) and
answers one question in plain language: who made this app, and has anyone
touched it since? It collects evidence from public Apple APIs and Apple
provided tools, then prints a short verdict.
.B \-\-details
prints the full evidence.
.PP
Disk images are mounted read only. Installer packages are expanded into a
temporary directory. The original target is never modified. waxen does not
remove quarantine attributes, change Gatekeeper settings, modify TCC
databases, disable system protections, re sign applications, install
certificates, or use the network.
.SH VERDICTS
.TP
.B trusted
Signed, unchanged since signing, and accepted by macOS.
.TP
.B cautious
Signed and unchanged, but not notarized, so macOS asks before opening it.
.TP
.B unsigned
No developer signature, or an ad hoc placeholder. macOS cannot tell who made it.
.TP
.B tampered
The contents no longer match the signature, or Apple revoked the certificate.
.TP
.B broken
The app is incomplete or packaged incorrectly and cannot run.
.TP
.B unknown
Not enough evidence was available to answer.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.I target
With no command, the same as
.BR diagnose .
.TP
.B diagnose
Print the verdict for an application bundle, disk image, or installer package.
.TP
.B evidence
Show the raw evidence without a diagnosis.
.TP
.B finder install
Add a Finder Quick Action named \(lqWhy Won\(cqt This Open?\(rq to
~/Library/Services. This is the only waxen command that writes to disk.
.TP
.B finder uninstall
Remove that Quick Action. waxen only removes a workflow it created.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-details
Print the full report: target, environment, bundle, findings, diagnosis, and
evidence.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Same as
.B \-\-details
plus suggested repair actions.
.TP
.B \-\-share
Print the verdict as Markdown for a GitHub issue or chat. Paths are reduced to
file names.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit a machine readable JSON report. The schema is unchanged by the verdict.
.TP
.B \-\-alert
Show the verdict in a macOS alert with a Copy Report button. Used by the
Finder Quick Action. Always exits 0.
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable colored output. Color is also off when output is not a terminal or
.B NO_COLOR
is set.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show usage information.
.TP
.B \-\-version, \-V
Print the waxen version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Inspection completed without a confirmed launch blocker.
.TP
.B 1
A confirmed launch blocker was found.
.TP
.B 64
Command usage error.
.TP
.B 65
Target type is outside the supported .app, .dmg, and .pkg scope.
.TP
.B 66
Target path does not exist.
.TP
.B 69
Required security evidence is unavailable.
.TP
.B 70
Internal tool error.
.TP
.B 73
The Finder Quick Action could not be installed or removed.
.TP
.B 77
Inspection is limited by permissions.
.TP
.B 78
Host is not a supported macOS environment. The GitHub Action uses this
when it would otherwise try to install waxen on a non-macOS runner.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check a download:
.PP
.RS
.nf
waxen ~/Downloads/MyApp.dmg
.fi
.RE
.PP
Paste the result into a bug report:
.PP
.RS
.nf
waxen ~/Downloads/MyApp.dmg --share | pbcopy
.fi
.RE
.PP
See all of the evidence:
.PP
.RS
.nf
waxen /Applications/MyApp.app --details
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add the Finder right-click action:
.PP
.RS
.nf
waxen finder install
.fi
.RE
.SH SUPPORTED PLATFORM
macOS 13 or newer. Application bundles (.app), disk images (.dmg), and
installer packages (.pkg) are supported. ZIP archives remain outside the
current scope.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR codesign (1),
.BR spctl (8),
.BR stapler (1),
.BR xattr (1)
